# Compose-level settings. Copy to /opt/udigity/.env (the repository root, next to docker-compose.prod.yml). Compose reads
# that file automatically, so these values survive a reboot, a new SSH session and a plain `docker compose up -d`.
# devops/scripts/deploy.sh writes UDIGITY_TAG for you; everything else has a working default. No secrets in this file.

# Image tag of the running release (git short sha). Required: compose refuses to start without it, so it can never fall back
# to an unknown "latest" image. Rollback = write the previous tag here and `up -d` (devops/DEPLOY.md section 12).
UDIGITY_TAG=

# Where the bundled nginx listens on the host. Loopback only: the server's existing proxy forwards to it (devops/proxy/*.example).
# HTTP_BIND must stay 127.0.0.1 (or the bridge address of a proxy that runs in Docker); never 0.0.0.0.
# HTTP_BIND=127.0.0.1
# HTTP_PORT=8080

# Pinned Docker networks (G-04). Change all together only if `docker network inspect $(docker network ls -q)` shows one of
# these ranges already used by another project on the server, and update TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS in backend.env to NGINX_INTERNAL_IP/32.
# UDIGITY_SUBNET_INTERNAL=172.29.10.0/24
# UDIGITY_SUBNET_PUBLIC=172.29.20.0/24
# UDIGITY_SUBNET_EGRESS=172.29.30.0/24
# NGINX_INTERNAL_IP=172.29.10.10

# Frontend build-time values (inlined into the browser bundle). Must equal PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH / CSRF_COOKIE_NAME in backend.env.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CSRF_COOKIE_NAME=__Host-udigity_csrf
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH=12
